Package: Rfishmorph
Type: Package
Title: Digitizing, Storing, Analysing and Exploring the FISHMORPH Database
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aurele", "Toussaint", email = "aurele.toussaint@cnrs.fr",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(affiliation = "CNRS")))
Description: Tools dedicated to the FISHMORPH morphological database (Brosse et
    al., 2021, Global Ecology and Biogeography). Rfishmorph reconstructs the 21
    FISHMORPH landmarks, computes the 11 body segments and the 9 dimensionless
    morphological ratios, standardizes landmark geometry and enforces the
    FISHMORPH digitizing conventions, projects specimens into the FISHMORPH
    functional trait space, and provides visualization and quality-control tools
    to compare segment- and landmark-derived measurements. It also offers a
    guided workflow to add new species, using 'rfishbase' to validate and update
    taxonomy and to build a global list of freshwater fishes. Two 'shiny'
    applications cover the ends of the workflow: a guided digitizer that turns
    specimen photographs into landmarks, and an explorer of the global
    morphological space of freshwater fishes. Digitized specimens are captured in
    an append-only journal and consolidated into a derived 'DuckDB' database with
    integrity constraints, from which 'Parquet' and CSV archives are exported. The
    FISHMORPH routines were originally developed inside 'intraitR' and are
    collected here as a stand-alone package.
